  "slug": "condensation-dynamics-e624",
  "summary": "Polymer simulations now infer chromatin dynamics from static Hi-C data and test how well microscopy constrains looping estimates.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the use of polymer models to connect chromosome structure, dynamics and mechanism. The Full-Inversion Chromatin model learns an effective force field from Hi-C contacts to infer yeast chromosome ensembles and locus-dependent dynamics across the cell cycle. A mesoscale jump-diffusion model of cohesin loop extrusion, parametrized from single-molecule data, explains stall force, kinetic phases and CTCF barrier function. A separate simulation study with ground truth shows that thresholding noisy 3D microscopy distances misestimates chromatin looping probability, lifetime and search time. The new elements are dynamical inference from static contact data and explicit validation of how well experimental readouts constrain looping.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
}
